# The runtime image only needs the gateway sources and the root helper; the
# `plugins` stage additionally needs the client sources it bundles. Both sets
# are listed below, and node_modules never comes along: the stage installs its
# own inside the build, which is what keeps every build host identical.
*
!Dockerfile
!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.*.json
!gateway/
!gateway/**
!bin/
!bin/**
!skills/
!skills/**
# Bundled inside the `plugins` stage; gateway/plugins.mjs ships the result into
# each user's profile.
!plugins/
!plugins/**
!packages/
!packages/**
!vendor/
!vendor/**
!scripts/
!scripts/**
# The plugins stage compiles the client project graph, which references the
# native addon package and the patched dependencies the lockfile names.
!native/
!native/**
!patches/
!patches/**
# The workspace install covers every workspace member, so each member's
# directory has to be in the context.
!apps/
!apps/**
!benchmarks/
!benchmarks/**
!website/
!website/**
!python/
!python/**
# Install output and build artifacts are regenerated in the stage.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.turbo
**/.tsbuildinfo
